            "type": "paragraph",
            "text": "Here is the core mechanic. An insurance company collects premiums from a large pool of policyholders. The vast majority of those policyholders never experience the worst-case event in any given year. The small percentage who do experience the event have their losses paid from the collective pool. The insurance company calculates the probability of these events, adds operating costs and profit margins, and prices the premium accordingly."
